WEBVTT

00:00:20.235 --> 00:00:23.058
This is Milestone 3, on the live Portal. It
begins where your work began: with the

00:00:23.118 --> 00:00:25.941
Registers.

00:00:26.009 --> 00:00:30.449
Sixty seven Fields, four hundred and ten
Specialties and the alias set, loaded from the

00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:34.949
documents you wrote, and now yours to maintain
without a developer.

00:00:42.139 --> 00:00:46.579
Here are the crowded neighbours. Public
Health, Health Policy, Public Policy, Public

00:00:46.639 --> 00:00:51.079
Administration. The line beside each is the
one that helps somebody choose.

00:00:51.724 --> 00:00:55.973
Renaming a term here changes every profile
that uses it at once. Retiring one stops

00:00:56.033 --> 00:01:00.282
offering it, and leaves it exactly where it
already is.

00:01:07.399 --> 00:01:12.113
A direct invitation, as in Milestone 2. Name
only, link copied, sent by hand.

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:22.746
Helena has registered, and this is what is
new. Her profile and the community are one

00:01:22.806 --> 00:01:25.753
click away.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:30.487
Her profile. Each part saves on its own,
because people do this over several sittings

00:01:30.547 --> 00:01:33.804
and often on a phone.

00:01:33.876 --> 00:01:38.316
And she is not yet in the directory. A profile
joins it once it carries a name, a title, a

00:01:38.376 --> 00:01:42.816
Field, and something in her own words. Nothing
is urgent.

00:01:46.597 --> 00:01:50.970
A photograph. Whatever shape arrives, it is
cropped to the centre and held to the same

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:55.403
portrait rectangle, so the directory reads
consistently.

00:01:58.421 --> 00:02:02.887
Her full title. One hundred and eighteen
characters, nothing abbreviated.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:09.609
Country is shown to collaborators. City stays
with the Institute. That was the promise made

00:02:09.669 --> 00:02:13.887
when it was asked for, and the screen says so.

00:02:16.841 --> 00:02:20.842
Up to three current positions, each with its
own organisation and department. Senior people

00:02:20.902 --> 00:02:24.903
hold more than one appointment at once.

00:02:30.052 --> 00:02:33.030
Where her work belongs. The orientation opens
by itself the first time and never interrupts

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:36.068
again.

00:02:36.139 --> 00:02:41.721
Classify lightly. Describe richly. She is not
being asked to describe everything she knows.

00:02:43.723 --> 00:02:48.685
Search first, never a list to scroll. Sixty
seven Fields are nothing to a search.

00:02:51.116 --> 00:02:54.032
Type the word you use. Physiotherapy leads to
Physical Therapy, and the screen quietly says

00:02:54.092 --> 00:02:57.008
why.

00:03:00.981 --> 00:03:04.827
A Specialty is optional. Selecting one never
assigns her a Field. A journalist who writes

00:03:04.887 --> 00:03:08.733
about health policy is a journalist.

00:03:09.607 --> 00:03:12.864
And no dead end. If nothing fits, she writes
the term she uses and carries on. The

00:03:12.924 --> 00:03:16.181
Institute decides later.

00:03:22.052 --> 00:03:27.138
Credentials after the name, up to three,
chosen from the library rather than typed.

00:03:28.479 --> 00:03:32.919
The same letters, several records. FRCP
differs between London, Edinburgh and Glasgow,

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:37.419
and the meaning beside each is how she picks
the one she holds.

00:03:40.554 --> 00:03:44.245
And the meaning is searchable as well as the
letters. Somebody who does not think of

00:03:44.305 --> 00:03:47.996
themselves as an MPH still finds it.

00:03:56.461 --> 00:04:00.710
Her profile as another collaborator sees it.
Credentials after the name. The full title,

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:05.019
wrapped rather than cut. City nowhere on the
page.

00:04:06.386 --> 00:04:10.826
Links show their label and never their
address. Empty sections do not appear at all,

00:04:10.886 --> 00:04:15.326
so a profile with a few things filled in reads
as deliberate.

00:04:16.535 --> 00:04:20.975
The directory. She appears because her profile
now says enough. Only Fields containing

00:04:21.035 --> 00:04:25.475
somebody are offered, so a small community
does not look deserted.

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:31.310
And from the footer of every page, somewhere
to say what she found. Your Alpha group are

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:35.712
the most valuable readers this Portal will
ever have.

00:04:52.328 --> 00:04:55.268
Helena proposed Longevity Economics as a
Field. It arrives here with anything close

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:58.268
that the vocabulary already holds, so mapping
is one click and a duplicate is hard to

00:04:58.328 --> 00:05:01.268
approve by accident.

00:05:01.788 --> 00:05:06.228
You may correct the wording before approving.
Because people select entries rather than

00:05:06.288 --> 00:05:10.728
typing text, your wording is what every
profile then shows, including hers.

00:05:12.333 --> 00:05:16.773
Approved. It is now in the vocabulary, on her
profile, and she has been told. Had you

00:05:16.833 --> 00:05:21.273
declined, nothing would have been sent:
whether to explain is yours.

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:25.636
What the community has said about the Portal,
with the page each person was on when they

00:05:25.696 --> 00:05:28.643
said it.

00:05:52.769 --> 00:05:56.119
Rafael, a geriatrician, searches for an
actuary and finds Helena. Two people who would

00:05:56.179 --> 00:05:59.529
not otherwise have met.

00:06:02.086 --> 00:06:05.026
What the first Beta uses instead of messaging.
He registers an interest, the Institute sees

00:06:05.086 --> 00:06:08.026
it and passes it on. A record and a note, not
a conversation, and only because Helena said

00:06:08.086 --> 00:06:11.026
she was open to approaches.

00:06:25.362 --> 00:06:29.673
And here it is on your side. One collaborator
would like to work with another. Passing it on

00:06:29.733 --> 00:06:34.044
is yours to do, which at Alpha is exactly
right.
